        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Listen first, then push the belt by
            hand.</strong> A motor that hums means something is jammed or the
            capacitor has failed — switch off within seconds. A motor that spins
            freely with no belt movement means the drive belt. A belt that turns
            normally by hand points at the electronics.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Rule out the free causes first — speed at zero, safety key, an object
            under the belt, an over-tight belt. If the machine is dead rather than
            unresponsive, start at
            <a href="/treadmill-wont-turn-on/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">will not turn on</a>,
            and prevent the next one with the
            <a href="/treadmill-maintenance/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">maintenance schedule</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
